# Line endings are LF in the repository and LF in the working tree, on every
# platform. Without this, Git for Windows checks files out with CRLF, and gofmt
# — which only ever emits LF — then reports every Go file in the tree as
# unformatted. That is not a style preference: it is the difference between the
# Windows CI job checking our formatting and failing before it runs a line of
# Windows code.
#
# Nothing here is built by a Windows-native toolchain that wants CRLF: the
# shell is Go, and the CI steps run under the bash that ships with Git.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary, so Git neither converts nor diffs them.
*.png binary
*.icns binary
*.pdf binary
